<Project>

  <!--
    A warning fails the build for everything that ships.

    The cold build has been clean for a while, and nothing held it there: NU1903 - a high-severity
    advisory in the native SQLite this ledger loads - sat in the output as a warning until someone
    happened to read it, and it had already shipped in dist\App by then. A warning nobody is forced
    to read is a finding nobody acts on.

    Deliberately here rather than at the repository root: coursework/ is a separate tree with its own
    owner, and whether a warning should stop a teaching lab is not this file's decision to make.

    To unblock a local experiment: dotnet build -p:TreatWarningsAsErrors=false. Do not commit that -
    fix the warning, or exempt exactly one code with WarningsNotAsErrors and say why.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
